      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "HANSADIOS (4) has the strongest recent case, having won at Ascot two starts back before running fourth in the Placid Ark Prelude, beaten a length and a half by Levati Dimezzo. She is third-up, race fit and already proven around 1000m. Looks primed for a bold showing back in this grade. NINETYMILESTRAIGHT (1) bring a black-type profile, missing in Listed level three back before a narrow defeat in Open 3YO company after that. She was out to 1800m before the break, so happy to overlook that effort and her recent trial suggests she's back on song. Live chance with the apprentice claim. ARTIE'S STORM (5) has been costly as favourite at her past two, yet the return to 1000m suits and her latest effort had merit after an awkward beginning. SHARPASSA (2) resumes off a mixed last campaign, but the Northam NMW1Y second to Bricini and a solid 1000m record keep her in the mix. SHE'S CAPITANA (3) gets Pike on board second-up and she looks an improver.",
